# Line-ending policy for flux-limiter
#
# This repo is developed on both Windows and Linux. These rules make line
# endings a property of the repository rather than of any one machine's
# core.autocrlf setting, so the working tree is identical everywhere.
#
#   * text=auto eol=lf  -> every text file is stored AND checked out with LF
#   * binary            -> never normalize; keep bytes exactly as committed
#
# To re-normalize an existing checkout after adding this file:
#   git add --renormalize .
#   git status            # should show nothing to commit if index was already LF

* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicitly mark binary types so they are never touched by normalization
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.tar binary
